.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# pdf2epub transient reports (regenerated by verify.py / restore.py)
workspace/*/verify-report.json

# graded-reader headless runner: LLM config + API keys (never commit)
ai-tools/graded-reader/headless/config.json
ai-tools/graded-reader/headless/secrets/*
!ai-tools/graded-reader/headless/secrets/README.md

# wallpaper-maker: the reader's address on your LAN, remembered between pushes
tools/wallpaper-maker/last-device.json

# tgbot: the Telegram token, who is allowed to talk to it, and the delivery
# queue. The queue is state, not history — deleting it loses whatever was
# waiting for the device and nothing else.
tools/tgbot/config.json
tools/tgbot/secrets/*
!tools/tgbot/secrets/README.md
tools/tgbot/state/*
!tools/tgbot/state/.gitkeep

# extras/fonts/ ships two families, and adding a third is a *licensing*
# decision, not a tidiness one. This repo is MIT with OFL fonts attributed in
# ATTRIBUTION.md; a family you build from a font you bought — or from anything
# whose licence forbids redistribution — must not be republished under it by a
# stray `git add`. Same shape as workspace/: ignore them all, allowlist
# deliberately, and add the attribution when you do.
#
# NaskhFull is the fourth line, and it earns it the same way the others do:
# Noto Naskh Arabic and Noto Sans are both SIL OFL, so redistributing bitmap
# conversions of them here is exactly what their licence permits — that, and
# nothing about how useful the font is, is why it may be allowlisted.
extras/fonts/*/
!extras/fonts/WenKaiFull/
!extras/fonts/WenZilla/
!extras/fonts/CrimKai/
!extras/fonts/NaskhFull/

# opds-server: local library paths + Basic-auth password (never commit)
tools/opds-server/config.json
tools/opds-server/secrets/*
!tools/opds-server/secrets/README.md

# workspace/ is yours, not the repo's: whatever you write, convert, or drop in
# here stays local. The exceptions are the committed samples — one per tool,
# each built by the current pipeline — which are the proof those tools work and
# the fixtures their self-tests read. Adding a sample to the repo means adding a
# line here, deliberately.
#
# One sample each, on purpose: a book built by a superseded version of a
# pipeline is not evidence that the pipeline works today, it is evidence about
# code that no longer exists. The earlier readers (journey-west, letter-writer,
# newyear-gift, twelve-zodiac, yugong-mountain) and conversions
# (el-espanol-de-oran, gurruminos) are retired on
# claude/graded-reader-setup-ermfsg and stay in history; this allowlist is
# already written for that state, so their directories disappear when it lands.
workspace/*
# graded-reader
!workspace/being-earnest/
# pdf2epub
!workspace/alcaldes-encontrados/
# wallpaper-maker — the one sample, not the folder. workspace/wallpapers/ is
# your drop zone, so it is un-ignored just far enough to reach that file and
# re-ignored immediately; anything else you put there stays yours.
!workspace/wallpapers/
workspace/wallpapers/*
!workspace/wallpapers/finally-some-peace.png
